originality_and_literature.contribution_.reason:
The submission adds genuine scientific content:
- a new, physically motivated normal-ordered staggered NNN ZZ coupling;
- a derived focusing NLSE for the staggered chain that includes a hard-core (Dyson) kinematic term and the resulting MI threshold eps_c=J^2/4Delta^2;
- full-Hilbert-space confirmation of the first-order Kerr coefficient;
- a sector-resolved explanation of why MI does not appear on 9-11 qubits.
Novelty is limited. The mapping machinery (Schrieffer-Wolff, spin-coherent / Holstein-Primakoff mean field, Bogoliubov MI) is standard, as the paper acknowledges. The Dyson kinematic interaction is known. The positive emulation result is a first-order self-phase-modulation check, and the targeted phenomenon (MI) is not captured.

